 "comment": "Where the sigil look puts an item's signs (lane sigils, round three, November 11; hand-written, the one home of these numbers). Read by MagicLooks.cs (MagicLooks.Sigils) and checked by tools/sigils/build-sigils.test.mjs. A PROPOSAL for Adam. Adam on round two: one big sign on every item 'is a little too much like superheroes'; then 'I don't know that everything needs to be in a circle... on the breast, in the center, in some kind of pattern, whether that's a vertical stripe or a horizontal stripe... small little logos, like on clothes... bottom right side, bottom left side, upper right side, upper left side. Think about like Nike symbols'. So each item rolls ONE spot from its part's list below, by the shares, from its own id (the same item always looks the same). A spot is a single sign ('sign') or a stripe of small signs ('stripe'). MagicLooks then checks the spot against the piece itself: rays from the front must meet one surface of the body (not a rim, boss, strap, buckle or a seam between two surfaces) with no step in depth, at the middle and round the edge of every sign. A spot that does not fit is moved toward the middle and made a little smaller, step by step; if it still does not fit, the item takes its next spot in its own rolled order.",
